Dynamic Programming:

 DP is an optimization technique used when:
   1) problem has overlapping subproblems
   2) problem has optimal substructure

   Instead of recomputing the same thing again and again, you store results and reuse them.
   solve smaller problems -> store results -> reuse them


Step to solve Dp problems:

    1)define dp state  => dp[i]
    2)Find recurrence
    3)Base case for smaller values
    4)choose approach
    5)optimize (reduce space)

shortcut to write any problem:
1) Try to represent the problem in terms of indexes
2) Do all possible stuffs on that
3) sum of all stuffs => count all possible ways
   min(all stuffs) => find min



1) memoization (top-down approach)
  Recursion + caching(stored results)
2)Tabulation (Bottom-up approach)
   Iterative
